    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d461">

                <pb facs="0707" n="1216" sameAs="frus:frus1948v05p2/pg1216"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">501.BB Palestine/7–1348: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Saudi Arabia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Childs</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >to the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">confidential</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Jidda</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1948-07-13T13:00:00+03:00">July 13, 1948—1 p.
                            m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>412. Legtel 406, 12th.<anchor n="1" xml:id="d461-f1"/> British Ambassador states
                    he received yesterday from FO verbal reply to his
                    representations in behalf SA acceptance prolongation truce. Reply characterized
                    Bernadotte proposals as being worse than <hi rendition="#italic">status quo
                        ante</hi> but said SAG would support with
                    Arab states acceptable prolongation. Trott said he had been authorized to make
                    strong representations including reminder that if Arabs rejected truce and UN
                    applied sanctions HMG would be unable to fulfill
                    its arms commitments to Arab states.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d461-f2"/>
                </p>
                <p>Pouched Arab capitals.</p>
                <p>Sent Department 412, repeated London 124.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Childs</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d461-f1" n="1" xml:id="d461-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d461-f2" n="2" xml:id="d461-f2-content">
                <p>Damascus, on July 12, reported a conversation with the Syrian Acting Foreign
                    Minister in which the latter insisted that Count Bernadotte had proved himself
                    pro-Zionist and that Syria would never consent to an extension of the truce
                    until the Mediator’s absurd proposals had been scrapped. (Telegram 439, 501.BB
                    Palestine/7–1248)</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
